threads.body:
[General] When the url has no database but does have query parameters, using `jdbcUrl.length()` here leaves the query string inside the host/port segment:

* `mysql:host:1234?user=u` -> `parsePort("1234?user=u")` returns null, so the port silently stays at the default 3306
* `mysql:host?user=u` -> host becomes `host?user=u`

Falling back to the `?` position when `/` is absent fixes both.

```suggestion
    // without a database the host/port segment ends at the query string, if any
    int urlEndLoc = dbLoc != -1 ? dbLoc : jdbcUrl.indexOf('?');
    int effectiveDbLoc = urlEndLoc != -1 ? urlEndLoc : jdbcUrl.length();
```

